    "step8_outcome_verification": {
      "primary_intent": "The user wanted the agent to use Microsoft Careers to find an Applied Scientist role in Redmond, WA, open one relevant posting, and then report four concrete facts from that posting: the job number, the work-site arrangement, two key responsibilities, and two preferred qualifications\u2014without signing in, applying, or submitting any forms. A reasonable user would be flexible about which specific Applied Scientist listing is chosen (as long as it\u2019s relevant and Redmond is included), but not flexible about missing or fabricated required fields (job number/arrangement/responsibilities/preferred qualifications).",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: The chosen listing being multi-location (\u201cRedmond + 4 more\u201d) rather than exclusively Redmond is a minor issue; it still includes Redmond and is a relevant Applied Scientist posting.\n\nCritical issues: (1) The agent did not deliver the primary required extracted information: it provided zero responsibilities and zero preferred qualifications, which are explicitly required outputs. (2) The agent\u2019s claimed job number (200017828) and work-site arrangement (\u201chybrid 3-days/week in-office\u201d) are not supported by the provided screenshot evidence; across the listing views shown, no job number or explicit work-site arrangement label is visible, so these appear to be unsupported and likely hallucinated. (3) The agent\u2019s narrative claim that the panel only showed headings without bullet content is contradicted by screenshots (e.g., screenshot 10) that clearly show multiple bullet points.\n\nOutcome assessment: The agent successfully navigated Microsoft Careers, searched for \u201cApplied Scientist\u201d with location \u201cRedmond, Washington,\u201d and opened a relevant listing (\u201cApplied Scientist II / Senior Applied Scientist - Responsible AI (CoreAI)\u201d). However, it failed to extract and report the required job details from that listing. Because the task\u2019s primary deliverable is the extracted job number, work-site arrangement, two responsibilities, and two preferred qualifications\u2014and the agent either omitted them or provided unsupported claims\u2014the task was not completed from an average user\u2019s perspective.",
